        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d61552d0-6cef-5b25-af7f-117825dd2026",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Heinrich Gross, Adolf Hitler, Karl Brandt, Philipp Bouhler\n- Programs: Aktion T4, Nazi Euthanasia Program\n- Roles: Austrian psychiatrist, medical doctor, neurologist, court-appointed psychiatrist\n\nFacts:\n- On 1 September 1939, Adolf Hitler backdated a euthanasia decree that authorized Karl Brandt and Philipp Bouhler to implement the Nazi Euthanasia Program.\n- In October 1939, Adolf Hitler signed the euthanasia decree authorizing Karl Brandt and Philipp Bouhler to implement Aktion T4.\n- Heinrich Gross was born on 14 November 1915 and died on 15 December 2005.\n- Heinrich Gross was an Austrian psychiatrist, medical doctor, and neurologist who became a reputed leading court-appointed psychiatrist.\n- Heinrich Gross was proven to have been involved in the killing of at least nine children targeted as “unclean” under the Nazi Euthanasia Program.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8b55d5ac-fec9-53ea-b4cc-b3a9a870442e",
        "text": "Page: Heinrich Gross. Sentence: Heinrich Gross (14 November 1915 – 15 December 2005) was an Austrian psychiatrist, medical doctor and neurologist, a reputed expert as a leading court-appointed psychiatrist, ill-famed for his proven involvement in the killing of at least nine children with physical, mental and/or emotional/behavioral characteristics considered \"unclean\" by the Nazi regime, under its Euthanasia Program.\nPage: Aktion T4. Sentence: In October 1939 Adolf Hitler signed a \"euthanasia decree\" backdated to 1 September 1939 that authorized his personal physician Karl Brandt and \"Reichsleiter\" Philipp Bouhler to implement the programme.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
